Day 296/300: Count Submatrices with Top-Left Element and Sum Less Than k

Problem Statement: #3070

Problem Statement EXplantion:

You are given a 0-indexed 2D integer matrix grid and an integer k.
Return the number of submatrices that contain the top-left element grid[0][0] and have a sum less than or equal to k.

Solution Approach:

Since every valid submatrix must include the top-left corner (0,0), we are essentially looking for all submatrices ending at any cell (i,j) such that the sum of the rectangle from (0,0) to (i,j) is ≤k.

Core Logic
We use the 2D Prefix Sum formula to calculate the sum of the submatrix ending at (i,j) in O(1) time by leveraging previously computed values:

S[i][j]=grid[i][j]+S[i−1][j]+S[i][j−1]−S[i−1][j−1]
Initialization: Create a 2D array prefixSum of size (rows+1)×(cols+1) to handle boundary cases (where i=0 or j=0) without extra if statements.

Iteration: Traverse the grid row by row.
Condition: If prefixSum[i][j] <= k, increment the counter.
Optimization: Since all elements in the grid are non-negative, if prefixSum[i][j] > k, then any further submatrix in the same row (to the right) will also exceed k. We can safely break the inner loop for that row.

Here's the Code:

class Solution {
    public int countSubmatrices(int[][] grid, int k) {
        int rows = grid.length;
        int cols = grid[0].length;
        int count = 0;
        int[][] prefixSum = new int[rows + 1][cols + 1];
        
        for (int i = 1; i <= rows; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= cols; j++) {
                prefixSum[i][j] = grid[i - 1][j - 1] 
                                + prefixSum[i - 1][j] 
                                + prefixSum[i][j - 1] 
                                - prefixSum[i - 1][j - 1];
                
                if (prefixSum[i][j] <= k) {
                    count++;
                } else {
                    break; 
                }
            }
        }
        
        return count;
    }
}

Complexity:

Time Complexity: O(M×N)
Space Complexity: O(M×N)






